SwissEphNet is a C-to-C# port of the Swiss Ephemeris Free Edition,
originally created by Yan Grenier (https://github.com/ygrenier/SwissEphNet),
2014-2019.

This repository (https://github.com/Tim81/SwissEphNet) is a maintained fork
of Yan Grenier's SwissEphNet, continuing that work. Since 2026 it has been
maintained by Timothy van der Ham, who modernized the build and target
frameworks and fixed a number of bugs in the port, including the fixed-star
search returning the wrong star, multi-word star names being unfindable,
the heliacal Moon branch never being taken, swe_set_astro_models throwing,
the DIR_GLUE path separator, culture-sensitive string comparison, and a
netstandard2.0 infinite recursion. See the changelog / release notes for
details.

